BT /F2 17 Tf 56 736 Td (What is a pointer?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 702 Td 15 TL
(A pointer is a variable that stores the memory address of another variable. If x is an int,) Tj T*
(then &x is the address of x, and a pointer to an int is declared with int *p.) Tj T*
T*
(To follow a pointer to the value it points to, use the dereference operator *. After p = &x,) Tj T*
(the expression *p means the same thing as x, so *p = 5 changes x to 5.) Tj T*
T*
(A pointer that points to nothing should be set to NULL. Dereferencing a NULL pointer crashes) Tj T*
(the program, so check a pointer against NULL before you use it when it might be empty.) Tj T*
ET
