BT /F2 17 Tf 56 736 Td (Pointers and arrays) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 702 Td 15 TL
(The name of an array, used in an expression, becomes a pointer to its first element. So for) Tj T*
(an array a, a[i] is exactly the same as *\(a + i\).) Tj T*
T*
(Pointer arithmetic. Adding 1 to a pointer moves it to the next element, not the next byte:) Tj T*
(if p points to an int and an int is 4 bytes, then p + 1 is 4 bytes further on. Subtracting) Tj T*
(two pointers into the same array gives the number of elements between them.) Tj T*
T*
(Strings in C are arrays of char that end with the character '\\0'. A function that receives a) Tj T*
(string receives a char pointer to its first character.) Tj T*
ET
