BT /F2 17 Tf 56 736 Td (Dynamic memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 702 Td 15 TL
(malloc\(n\) asks for n bytes on the heap and returns a pointer to them, or NULL if it fails.) Tj T*
(Always check the result. calloc\(count, size\) does the same but sets every byte to zero.) Tj T*
(realloc\(p, n\) changes the size of an earlier allocation and may move it.) Tj T*
T*
(free\(p\) gives the memory back. Every malloc should have exactly one matching free.) Tj T*
(Forgetting to free causes a memory leak, and freeing the same pointer twice \(a double free\)) Tj T*
(corrupts the heap and can crash the program.) Tj T*
T*
(After calling free\(p\), set p to NULL. Using memory after it has been freed is called a use-) Tj T*
(after-free bug, and the pointer is then a dangling pointer.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56 40 Td (Introduction to C Pointers: Study Notes \(sample document\)  -  Page 4 of 5) Tj ET
endstream
