BT /F2 17 Tf 56 736 Td (Common mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 702 Td 15 TL
(Using an uninitialised pointer. A pointer declared with no value contains garbage, so) Tj T*
(dereferencing it is undefined behaviour. Initialise pointers to NULL or to a valid address.) Tj T*
T*
(Returning the address of a local variable. The variable disappears when the function) Tj T*
(returns, so the pointer dangles. Return allocated memory or pass in a buffer instead.) Tj T*
T*
(Off-by-one errors. An array of n elements has valid indexes 0 to n - 1. Writing to index n) Tj T*
(overruns the array.) Tj T*
T*
(sizeof on a pointer. For an array a, sizeof\(a\) is the size of the whole array, but for a) Tj T*
(pointer p, sizeof\(p\) is only the size of the pointer itself, usually 8 bytes.) Tj T*
T*
(Practice question: what does **pp = 7 do if pp is an int ** that points to a pointer p that) Tj T*
(points to an int x? It sets x to 7.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56 40 Td (Introduction to C Pointers: Study Notes \(sample document\)  -  Page 5 of 5) Tj ET
